17.6 Architectural Bottlenecks, SPOF Mitigation, and Recovery
SPOF & Connection Saturation (NFR-004): Connection exhaustion is mitigated via a managed connection pool (src/config/database.js) enforcing max: 20, a 2,000 ms acquisition timeout, and a 30-second idle connection reclamation.

Disaster Recovery (RPO & PITR): PostgreSQL Write-Ahead Logging (WAL) and automated snapshots provide point-in-time recovery to reconstruct committed transactions without data corruption.

Concurrency Control (FR-005, FR-006): Optimistic Concurrency Control (OCC) is enforced using timestamp version checking (WHERE request_id = :id AND updated_at = :last_seen_timestamp), rejecting race conditions with HTTP 409 Conflict.
